  "notes": "Opium duo — \"snotty hip-hop with Slipknot aesthetics\". Aggressive driving kicks at a higher density than the plugg-derived rage lanes, crash washes, and 808s that PUNCH rather than glide: `slideProb` is deliberately low where the rest of this cohort runs high, because the research says \"little melodic sliding — more static punch\". Sparse hats. Minimal chord movement — 1-2 bar loops with tritone-flavoured riffing. 406/500 distinct. ⚠ `every_mood_of_every_genre_reaches_the_variety_floor` measured this model under rage’s inherited `sparse` mood — which clamps the melody to 1-3 notes a bar with a 0.6 empty-bar bias — and it fell short of 500 distinct melodies in 1000 seeds. ⛔ The cure is a 4-bar phrase option at low weight, NOT a change of character: a one-bar phrase repeats four times in four bars, so excluding 4 entirely was a stronger claim than the research makes. The research describes the CHORD loop as short; the melody’s phrasing is a separate field, and the ostinato still dominates by weight.",
